From 48bd050baef44802b1f052cbb46006d6325acbf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(front): fail on a configuration number past TLC's
 integers as TLC's parseInt does

ModelConfig.parseValue reads a number with Integer.parseInt as it
parses the configuration, before the spec, and the
NumberFormatException it throws on one past 2147483647 escapes as an
exception TLC didn't expect: it prints message 1000 with the
exception and exits 255. The front end checked the number once it had
the spec and reported an overflow of its own with exit 75. It now
fails as it parses the configuration, with TLC's words. The 12 runs
of the upstream conformance suite with such a number print what the
pinned TLC prints; the suite's expected output for them is its own
correction, not TLC's.

The library still declines such a check, since TLC's unexpected
exception is no TlaConfigError: its reason now gives the exit 255 the
check exits with. A test that logs a declined check with what it
reads declined at this number, which the check now rejects before it
reads a module, so it declines at a constant definition TLC computes
as it starts instead.
